  "observations": [
    "For memory cases, raw/scalar BER remains near random-decision levels as SNR rises because temporal memory distortion dominates AWGN.",
    "The 7-tap equalizer reduces BER substantially for exponential and two-scale memory at high SNR, but does not fully invert the power-law case.",
    "Scalar gain compensation is insufficient for these memory transformations.",
    "Identity is an AWGN sanity baseline; at 20–30 dB its BER is zero in this finite test set."
  ],
  "caveat": "These results test receiver-side compensability; they do not establish an intrinsic communication advantage for MIN."
